WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:12.282
Hi! Which fruit do pupils like best? In a picture graph, one picture can stand for 2 pupils. Today we'll read picture graphs with scales.

2
00:00:12.432 --> 00:00:16.842
First read the key: each circle stands for 2 pupils.

3
00:00:16.992 --> 00:00:22.794
Apple has 4 circles. 4 twos are 8, so 8 pupils like apples.

4
00:00:22.944 --> 00:00:27.930
Banana has 6 circles. 6 twos are 12 pupils.

5
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:34.074
Orange has 3 circles. 3 twos are 6 pupils.

6
00:00:34.224 --> 00:00:39.042
Which is the most popular? Look for the longest row: banana.

7
00:00:39.192 --> 00:00:44.826
How many more pupils like bananas than apples? 12 minus 8 is 4.

8
00:00:44.976 --> 00:00:50.754
How many pupils altogether? 8 plus 12 plus 6 is 26.

9
00:00:50.904 --> 00:00:58.098
If one picture stands for 5 or 10, multiply by 5 or 10 instead.

10
00:00:58.248 --> 00:01:03.594
Watch out! Counting 4 circles and saying 4 pupils is wrong!

11
00:01:03.744 --> 00:01:08.610
Each circle stands for 2 pupils, so work out 4 times 2.

12
00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:12.666
So 8 pupils like apples.

13
00:01:12.816 --> 00:01:24.594
Your turn! Each circle is 2 pupils. Orange has 3 circles. How many pupils? Pause and think.

14
00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:30.186
3 twos are 6 pupils. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:30.336 --> 00:01:42.090
Another one! Each picture stands for 5 books. There are 4 pictures. How many books? Pause and think.

16
00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.514
4 fives are 20 books. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:47.664 --> 00:01:58.266
Here's another! Each circle is 2 people. How many circles for 10 people? Pause and think.

18
00:01:58.416 --> 00:02:05.010
10 divided by 2 is 5, so 5 circles. Did you get it right?

19
00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:16.194
Try one more! 12 like bananas and 6 like oranges. How many more like bananas? Pause and think.

20
00:02:16.344 --> 00:02:22.074
12 minus 6 is 6 more. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:22.224 --> 00:02:33.258
Try one more! Apple 8, banana 12, orange 6. Which is the least popular? Pause and think.

22
00:02:33.408 --> 00:02:40.194
Orange has the fewest pictures, only 6 pupils. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:40.344 --> 00:02:52.146
Last one! Each picture stands for 10 cars. There are 3 pictures. How many cars? Pause and think.

24
00:02:52.296 --> 00:02:57.714
3 tens are 30 cars. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:57.864 --> 00:03:04.362
Remember: read the key first. The number of pictures times the key gives the real number.

26
00:03:04.512 --> 00:03:09.594
Do a survey with your family and draw a picture graph!

